  "authored_scope": "Supported: colour counts 3..9; horizontal periods 2..15 (default 3..9); random minimal row tiles; 1..8 non-overlapping 1-rectangles from 2x2 to 6x6, sometimes flush-touching to form L-shaped blobs; grids 4..30 per side. The native size 22x25 is used about half the time; other sizes are synthetic extensions. Explicit latent controls (num_colors, base, masks, width, height) reconstruct the fixtures exactly. Partial controls are honoured, or rejected with ValueError. Not supported: n=2 (no recoverable period); masks of colours other than 1; overlapping masks; scenes where any non-1 residue class is fully hidden. Default random generation never replays or looks up fixtures.",
  "authored_constraints": [
    "Every horizontal shift shorter than px and every vertical shift shorter than n shows a visible contradiction between two non-1 cells.",
    "Shifts px and n each have at least one comparable pair of non-1 cells.",
    "Every residue class whose true colour is not 1 keeps an unmasked witness.",
    "At least one masked cell has a true colour other than 1, so the input differs from the output.",
    "Random masks also cover at least one genuine 1, which stays 1 in the output.",
    "Masks never overlap and stay inside the grid.",
    "n < height and px < width; base is minimally cyclic and uses colours in 1..n."
  ],
